---
import Figure from "@/components/Figure.astro";
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const photos = [
  {
    src: "/images/about/matt-studio-portrait.webp",
    alt: "Matt smiling in a tan jacket.",
    width: 720,
    height: 720,
    className: "photo-primary",
  },
  {
    src: "/images/about/matt-with-camera.webp",
    alt: "Matt photographing outside with a camera.",
    width: 720,
    height: 720,
    className: "photo-secondary",
  },
  {
    src: "/images/about/dog-on-blanket.webp",
    alt: "Matt's dog sitting on a striped blanket.",
    width: 560,
    height: 560,
    className: "photo-support",
  },
  {
    src: "/images/about/courtroom-set.webp",
    alt: "Matt standing at a courtroom set podium.",
    width: 560,
    height: 560,
    className: "photo-support",
  },
  {
    src: "/images/about/pickleball-medals.webp",
    alt: "Matt and a teammate with pickleball medals.",
    width: 560,
    height: 560,
    className: "photo-support",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="About Matt, a product designer currently in Savannah, GA."
>
  <section class="site-container about-page" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <div class="about-back prose-flow">
      <a class="back-link" href="/" data-skip-home-flash>Back to home</a>
    </div>

    <div class="photo-grid" aria-label="Photos from Matt's work and life">
      {
        photos.map((photo, index) => (
          <div class:list={["about-photo", photo.className]}>
            <Figure
              src={photo.src}
              alt={photo.alt}
              width={photo.width}
              height={photo.height}
              loading={index < 2 ? "eager" : "lazy"}
              priority={index === 0}
            />
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <div class="about-intro prose-flow">
      <h1 id="about-title" class="h2">
        Hey, my name&rsquo;s Matt and I love product design
      </h1>
      <p>
        I came to design from a background in tech sales, photography, and
        computer science.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-container about-story" aria-label="Matt's story">
    <div class="prose-flow">
      <h2>My Story</h2>
      <p>
        Growing up, I always loved the cross between technology and business. In
        high school, I was an affiliate marketer. I made an army of Instagram
        bots and promoted a wide-range of offers from MaxBounty.
      </p>
      <p>
        In college, I went to Virginia Tech and majored in Business Information
        Technology. I started &ldquo;Blockchain at Virginia Tech&rdquo;, which
        quickly grew to over 370+ members. We traveled and competed in hackathons
        across the country. Dylan Love, the former head of content at
        <a href="https://cointelegraph.com/">Cointelegraph</a>, found my website
        and offered me a job. I started writing technical blogs, articles and
        press releases for crypto companies.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also worked directly with the Nirat Keswani, CEO of Empiric.io (now
        <a href="https://www.procense.ai/">Procense.ai</a>). As an account
        development representative, I built pipeline, improved product messaging
        and found their first enterprise contract, Tyson Foods.
      </p>
      <p>
        My career started at <a href="https://www.dell.com/">Dell</a>. I moved to
        Austin, TX and worked there for almost 3 years. As an Account Executive,
        I found, led and closed over $1.2M in new business data center sales (and
        $3.2M in total). I sold servers, SANs/NAS, APEX Backup Service (SaaS) and
        APEX as-a-service solutions. I also redesigned an internal VBA/Excel tool
        to automate emails and calendar invites, all in an intuitive user
        interface that encouraged my teammate&rsquo;s to use it. On average, it
        saved each team 10+ hours each week.
      </p>
      <p>
        Lastly, I decided to pursue my masters in computer science online at
        Virginia Tech. My dad&rsquo;s a disabled veteran (and an amazing dad),
        which means I had college benefits but they expired when I turned 27. So,
        I decided to part ways with Dell and focus on learning my craft. I also
        had a calling to live in LA. That&rsquo;s also where I learned about
        background acting. If you don&rsquo;t know, most of the time spent doing
        background is in &ldquo;holding&rdquo;, where you can do whatever you
        want. So, I would take my laptop, practice coding and work in the film
        industry. This led to me growing on TikTok, working as a photographer and
        eventually getting signed as a commercial actor with the
        <a href="https://www.theoptionagency.com/">TheOptionAgency.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Why I Love Design</h2>
      <p>
        During my masters, my favorite classes were UI Design, AI Prompt
        Engineering and Project Management (Jira). I love seeing how users
        interact with UIs, engineering design systems for agents and coming up
        with new features. It also tied in with my experience in sales, like
        listening to customers, managing stakeholders and driving the
        bottom-line.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-page {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--gap-content-block);
    padding-block: var(--gap-section);
  }

  .photo-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--spacing-150);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin-inline: auto;
    max-width: min(100%, calc(var(--measure-prose) - var(--spacing-1600)));
  }

  .about-photo {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .photo-primary,
  .photo-secondary {
    grid-column: span 3;
  }

  .photo-support {
    grid-column: span 2;
  }

  .about-photo :global(.figure),
  .about-photo :global(picture) {
    height: 100%;
  }

  .about-photo :global(.figure img) {
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-surface-muted);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .about-back,
  .about-intro {
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .about-intro h1 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 44px;
    place-items: center;
  }

  .about-story {
    padding-block: 0 var(--gap-hero);
  }

  .about-story .prose-flow {
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .photo-grid {
      gap: var(--spacing-100);
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    .photo-primary,
    .photo-secondary,
    .photo-support {
      grid-column: span 1;
    }

    .photo-support:last-child {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }

    .photo-support:last-child :global(.figure img) {
      aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    }
  }
</style>
